branchOpT -- SEQ 603 (Tony, 2026-11-10): BRANCh is the parent of four fixed shapes, each an operator built by the default
action: BREAk (op breakSignal), CONTINUe (continueSignal), RETURn (returnSignal) and RETURNVALUe (returnValue). The
keyword hands nothing up; the shape's op carries the signal; return's value is the one slot of its shape.

Not run alone: pop.sh runs each row twice, plain and with jitterRule(BRANCh); ahead of it, one process each under an
alarm. Each value reads: [stdout, lines joined by |] r<REFUSED lines> x<exit> s<sentinel>. The compiled arm must equal the
plain arm, and its door line is read beside it: built and fired summed over the four shapes.

BO-1  break in a block in a while.
BO-2  continue in a while.
BO-3  return with a value, in a new-road action body: 2 is not printed and the caller gets 5.
BO-4  a bare return, in a new-road action body: 2 is not printed.
BO-5  top level through FILe: break, continue and return each refuse by name and the next statement runs (R2).

ROWS, separated by ^ -- id ^ statements ^ value ^ built fired summed over the four shapes, compiled
BO-1^it1 = STARt("while 1; { print 1:; break; }"); testOP(it1); print 9:;^[1 |9 |] r0 x0 s1^1 1
BO-2^it1 = STARt("while qz < 3; { qz = qz + 1; if qz == 2; continue; print qz:; }"); testOP(it1); print 9:;^[1 |3 |9 |] r0 x0 s1^1 1
BO-3^boNew(boV); qr = boV(); print qr:; print 9:;^[1 |5 |9 |] r0 x0 s1^1 1
BO-4^boNew(boR); boR(); print 9:;^[1 |9 |] r0 x0 s1^1 1
BO-5^it1 = FILe("break;"); it1 = FILe("continue;"); it1 = FILe("return 5;"); it1 = FILe("return;"); print 9:;^[9 |] r4 x0 s1^4 4
